# `yo fix <path> --migrate mut-bindings` (plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md
# decision 47, step 2): a binding below module level is immutable unless
# declared `mut(name)`, so every local, typed, pattern, destructuring and
# compile-time binding written after its definition (reassigned, a field or
# element write, a `&mut` lend, a `&mut self` call) gets the marker (E0917
# otherwise). A collection handle mutated through its methods (`names`) and a
# binding only read (`fixed`) stay unmarked; the write of the by-value
# parameter `p` is listed, to rebind by hand. The dry run writes nothing; the
# expected_tree pins the rewritten main.yo, and the trailing `check` proves
# the result evaluates.
stdout_keep=^fix:|^error|E0917
timeout=240
